# udev rules for OpenFTIR spectrometer instruments
# Copy to /etc/udev/rules.d/99-openftir.rules and reload with:
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#   sudo udevadm trigger

# TEMPLATE: Replace VID and PID below with values from your instrument
# To find the VID:PID, run: tools/probe_instrument.py
# or: lsusb | grep -i "your-instrument-name"

# Example for Nicolet Summit (Thermo, USB interface):
# Uncomment and set the correct VID (vendor ID) and PID (product ID)
# SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="XXXX", ATTRS{idProduct}=="YYYY", MODE="0666", GROUP="plugdev", TAG="uaccess"

# Generic libusb-based instrument (example):
# SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0xYYYY", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0xZZZZ", GROUP="plugdev", TAG="uaccess"

# Instructions:
# 1. Plug in your spectrometer
# 2. Run: lsusb
# 3. Find your instrument in the list, note its Vendor ID (before colon) and Product ID (after colon)
# 4. Edit this file and uncomment/add a line with your VID and PID
# 5. Save and reload: sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
# 6. Unplug and replug the device
# 7. Test with: openftir-gui or python -m openftir.cli list-instruments
